{
  "title": "Burn down remaining one-off private Python helper imports",
  "description": "After the larger subsystem issues land, a small set of one-off private imports will still remain and should be cleaned up rather than left behind forever. Current stragglers include `_DECK_TYPE_TO_FORMAT_DIR` in `puppeteer/deck_choice.py`, `_generate_player_name` in `scripts/tournament_game.py`, `_coerce_snapshot` in `schemas/migrations/v7_to_v8.py`, and any leftover entries in the private-API allowlist once the bigger clusters are addressed.\n\
\n\
This should be the mop-up pass that gets the ratchet close to zero debt: remove the last underscore imports, make any truly shared helpers public in their owner module, and delete the corresponding allowlist entries from the weird-conventions test.\n\
\n\
Scope:\n\
- `puppeteer/src/puppeteer/config.py`\n\
- `puppeteer/src/puppeteer/deck_choice.py`\n\
- `scripts/tournament_game.py`\n\
- `schemas/migrations/v7_to_v8.py`\n\
- `schemas/game_export_types.py`\n\
- `puppeteer/tests/test_weird_conventions.py`",
